 "intro": "Rhandeia in Armenia, autumn 62 AD. You are Lucius Caesennius Paetus, newly sent to Armenia, who mocks Corbulo’s caution.",
 "debrief": "In Tacitus’s account, Paetus failed to stock his winter camp and scattered his troops to hold the passes. When Vologases came, the detachments were cut up and Paetus was besieged. Though Corbulo was only days away, he agreed to leave Armenia; his army was humiliated. Nero mocked Paetus and gave Corbulo full command. Peace came when Tiridates went to Rome to receive his crown from Nero. The other choices are what-ifs.",
